# CODEOWNERS -- GitHub auto-assigns reviewers for any PR that touches
# files matching a pattern below. Keep the default-owner rule first so
# new files inherit it; specific overrides go BELOW.
#
# Pattern syntax: <pattern>  <owner1> [<owner2> ...]
#   - Names must be GitHub usernames or org names (no @ prefix).
#   - Patterns are relative to repo root unless they start with /.
#   - One owner per line (we only have one maintainer org as of v0.1.1).
#
# Maintainer: @d33pstatetech-stack (sole owner of the org at this time).

# Default: every path -> maintainer org.
# Per GitHub's CODEOWNERS spec, a bare `*` (no slash) is the canonical
# "match every file in the repo" pattern. The slash-anchored variants
# (`/`, `/*`, `/**`) have narrower matching rules -- `/*` only matches
# the immediate root contents, not nested paths. Stick with bare `*`
# for the default. Specific overrides below TAKE PRECEDENCE over this
# default (last-matching rule wins per GitHub).
*                                               @d33pstatetech-stack

# Workflows: org owns them AND gets pinged first for CI changes.
/.github/workflows/                              @d33pstatetech-stack

# Server-side render pipeline: any change here affects exported MP4s.
/server/                                         @d33pstatetech-stack

# Composition source: any change here affects every rendered frame.
/compositions/                                   @d33pstatetech-stack

